  "description": "2026 wasn’t business as usual for Afrojack. Yes, there were familiar festivals like Untold in Romania and Ultra’s flagship Miami bash (alongside European and South African editions). And we got plenty of main-stage-scale releases, like “golden-era EDM”-style collab ‘Awake Tonight’, with Sia and David Guetta, that remix of Miley Cyrus’ ‘Wrecking Ball’, and ‘Alone’ alongside Mike Williams. But then there were also 10-hour sets under his Kapuchon alias, cuts on Loco Dice’s Desolat, lifestyle magazine covers spotlighting his relationship with Elettra Lamborghini, a near-death car crash, and a return to intimate gigs like the 400-capacity London “showclub”, REIGN.",
